course: dictionary
lesson: 9590
title: Many meanings of strength
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings. The context, meaning the words and sentences around it, tells you which meaning the writer wants. «The walrus used its two long tusks to haul itself onto the ice and to show strength.» Here strength means how strong a body is, the power to lift and pull.
explain: «Changing your mind when you hear a good reason is a strength.» Strength does not mean muscles here. It means a good quality, something a person does well. Try your meaning in the sentence: "Changing your mind when you hear a good reason is a good quality." It still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
explain: When you meet strength, ask: is this about power, about how much something can take, or about something a person is good at? The clues in the sentence will point to the answer. If you are still unsure, check a dictionary.
fact: Strength means how strong someone or something is.
fact: Strength can mean how much force something can take without breaking.
fact: Your strengths are the things you are good at.
fact: Strength can also mean courage and the power to keep going when things are hard.
fact: «Asking for help is a strength» means asking for help is a good quality.
exercise: «Asking for help is a strength.» In this sentence, strength means | Shouting very loudly | *A good quality, something you do well | How heavy something is | A rope that will not snap
exercise: Which word means the things you are good at? | Strangers | Weaknesses | *Strengths
exercise: Steel is stronger than plastic. Which meaning of strength is this? | Courage to keep going when things are hard | Your things you are good at | *How much force something can take without breaking
test: «The walrus used its two long tusks to haul itself onto the ice and to show strength.» Here strength means | Something you are good at | *The power of the body, how strong it is | Courage to keep going when things are hard
test: Ben says strengths and weaknesses mean the same thing. What is the right answer? | No, strengths are the things that break under force | Yes, the two words mean the same | *No, strengths are what you do well and weaknesses are what you need to improve
exam: Which meaning of strength is used in «Changing your mind when you hear a good reason is a strength»? | Muscle power | How much force a material can take | *A good quality, showing you care more about what is true
